course: dictionary
lesson: 1266
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A bus is a big road vehicle that carries many people, often on a set route with stops. Context tells you which meaning is meant. «Picture one wet bus stop with the bus twenty minutes late» is about a bus that is running behind time, not a bus that has broken down.
explain: Bus can also be a verb. «To bus people» means to take them somewhere by bus. A school might bus children to a museum. Look at the words around it to check which job the word is doing.
explain: The same bus can be called different things in different kinds of talk. «Catch the bus» and «catch the 12» are everyday talk, where 12 is the bus number. A notice might say «passengers boarding» instead, which means getting on. Read the sentence, then ask: is this chatty talk or a formal notice?
fact: A bus is a big road vehicle for many passengers, often on a set route with stops.
fact: A school bus takes children to and from school.
fact: To bus people means to take them somewhere by bus.
fact: A coach is a long-distance bus with luggage space underneath and seat belts for passengers.
fact: «Boarding» means getting on a bus, and «alighting» means getting off.
exercise: «Picture one wet bus stop with the bus twenty minutes late.» What is a bus stop? | A road closed for repairs | A kind of umbrella | *A place where buses stop so people can get on and off | A shop that sells bus tickets
exercise: Jack says «Oh brilliant, best day ever» when the bus is late. What does he really mean? | He is counting the passengers | He is asking for a bus ticket | He is delighted that the bus is late | *He is annoyed, and he does not mean it
exercise: «The school will bus the children to the museum.» What does bus mean here? | *To take them by bus | To hit them | To paint them yellow | To count them
test: «A girl in Dublin always left in a rush and ran across the road to catch the bus.» What did she do to catch the bus? | She waited at home | She bought a van | *She ran across the road to reach it | She sent a letter to the driver
test: What does alighting mean on a bus? | Paying the fare | Getting on | Waiting at the stop | *Getting off
exam: What is a coach? | *A long-distance bus with seat belts and luggage space | A small car for two people | A bus stop shelter | A type of envelope
